From f14e30ce3c4323b1d74d473b8ace3339adb30391 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 14:49:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: decompressor: Disable SCTLR.UWXN and SCTLR.WXN on armv7
 MMU enable

The bits 19 and 20 of the register SCTLR were reported as reserved
RAZ/SBZP in the ARM DDI 0406 Architecture Reference Manual ARMv7-A
and ARMv7-R till version B of the manual.

From version C, for devices with Virtualization Extension the two
bits get new functionality:
- SCTLR.WXN, bit[19], if set forces regions with write permission
  as XN (execute never);
- SCTLR.UWXN, bit[20], if set forces regions with write permission
  as XN for PL1 accesses.

The kernel decompressor will crash for fetch abort if an element
in the boot chain has set one of these two bits.

Clear the bits SCTLR.UWXN and SCTLR.WXN before enabling the MMU on
armv7.

Signed-off-by: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Ibd78619764b6b425e88cee891b9a1f1fdb4a6005
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/566555
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
@@ -886,6 +886,7 @@ __armv7_mmu_cache_on:
 						@ (needed for ARM1176)
 #ifdef CONFIG_MMU
  ARM_BE8(	orr	r0, r0, #1 << 25 )	@ big-endian page tables
+		bic	r0, r0, #3 << 19	@ clear SCTLR.UWXN and SCTLR.WXN
 		mrcne   p15, 0, r6, c2, c0, 2   @ read ttb control reg
 		orrne	r0, r0, #1		@ MMU enabled
 		movne	r1, #0xfffffffd		@ domain 0 = client
